## Model card

- **Name:** Claude Opus 4.7
- **Short description:** Anthropic’s Claude Opus 4.7 (released April 16, 2026) is a legacy Opus model for advanced software engineering and agentic work, with improved vision and 1M-token context, succeeded by newer Opus generations. Benchmark tables in accessible announcement text were not fully extractable in this pass.
- **Provider / access:** Anthropic Claude API `claude-opus-4-7`; available on Bedrock, Google Cloud, Microsoft Foundry, and Claude Platform on AWS per platform docs. No confirmed OpenCode Zen Free ID (`noFreeId` in local metadata).
- **Release / knowledge:** Released April 16, 2026. Reliable/training knowledge cutoff January 2026 (platform docs).
- **IDs:** `claude-opus-4-7`, `anthropic.claude-opus-4-7` (Bedrock). Local metadata ID `opencode/claude-opus-4.7`.
- **Context window:** 1M tokens context, 128K max output (300K batch beta supported per docs).
- **Modalities:** Text and image input; text output (improved high-resolution vision noted in announcement).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** Paid tier — $5 / 1M input, $25 / 1M output (per announcement/docs).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary Anthropic model; architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

